    {"id": "Q1", "text": "To what extent does expressed frustration regarding the lack of third-party debate presence correlate with an individual's likelihood of supporting non-voting as a form of protest?"},
    {"id": "Q2", "text": "How does the combination of advocating for libertarian policies and expressing opinions on climate change policy (either praise or criticism) influence an individual's predicted voting preference?"},
    {"id": "Q3", "text": "What is the relationship between expressing views on immigration reform and championing social justice initiatives, and how does this relate to predicted voting preference?"},
    {"id": "Q4", "text": "Does consistent criticism of the two-party system, particularly when reacting to specific political events (e.g., government shutdowns, Supreme Court decisions), reliably predict a specific voting preference?"},
    {"id": "Q5", "text": "How does the endorsement of a specific candidate (Democratic or Republican) interact with expressed opinions on issues like gun rights or universal healthcare to shape overall voting behavior?"},
    {"id": "Q6", "text": "What is the predictive power of consistently expressing views on specific policies (e.g., tax cuts for corporations, bipartisan infrastructure bills) in conjunction with endorsements of political candidates?"}
  ]
}

